---
import DevLayout from '../../layouts/DevLayout.astro';
---

<DevLayout
  title="Developer Guide - Salesdam"
  description="Technical documentation for Salesdam developers"
>
  <h1>Developer Guide</h1>

  <p>
    Welcome to the Salesdam Developer Guide. This documentation is intended for
    developers who want to understand the technical architecture, contribute to
    the codebase, or build custom integrations.
  </p>

  <div class="warning">
    <strong>Internal Documentation:</strong> This guide contains technical implementation
    details and is intended for development team members and technical stakeholders.
  </div>

  <h2>What's Covered</h2>

  <p>This guide provides in-depth technical documentation covering:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Architecture:</strong> System design, technology stack, and folder structure
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Authentication:</strong> Session management, middleware, and API key
      authentication
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Data Model:</strong> Database schemas, relationships, and entity diagrams
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Features:</strong> Implementation details for each major feature
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>API Reference:</strong> Complete endpoint documentation with examples
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>User Stories:</strong> Backlog of user stories, acceptance criteria,
      and test cases
    </li>

    <h2>Technology Stack</h2>

    <h3>Backend</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Runtime:</strong> Node.js 18+</li>
      <li><strong>Framework:</strong> Express.js 4.x</li>
      <li><strong>Database:</strong> MongoDB 6.0+ with Mongoose ODM</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Session Store:</strong> MongoDB sessions with connect-mongo
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Authentication:</strong> Session-based with bcrypt for password hashing
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Frontend</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Framework:</strong> React 18</li>
      <li><strong>Build Tool:</strong> Vite</li>
      <li><strong>Styling:</strong> CSS Modules + CSS Variables</li>
      <li><strong>State Management:</strong> React Context API</li>
      <li><strong>HTTP Client:</strong> Axios</li>
      <li><strong>Routing:</strong> React Router v6</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Development Tools</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Version Control:</strong> Git</li>
      <li><strong>Package Manager:</strong> npm</li>
      <li><strong>Code Quality:</strong> ESLint</li>
      <li><strong>API Testing:</strong> Postman/Insomnia</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Quick Start</h2>

    <h3>Prerequisites</h3>
    <pre><code>- Node.js 18 or higher
- MongoDB 6.0 or higher
- npm or yarn
- Git</code></pre>

    <h3>Installation</h3>
    <pre><code># Clone repository
git clone https://github.com/SaphoM/Salesdam-v3.git
cd Salesdam-v3

# Install backend dependencies
cd backend
npm install

# Install frontend dependencies
cd ../frontend
npm install</code></pre>

    <h3>Configuration</h3>
    <pre><code># Backend .env file (backend/.env)
PORT=5000
MONGO_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017/salesdam
SESSION_SECRET=your-secret-key-here
NODE_ENV=development

# Frontend .env file (frontend/.env)
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:5000</code></pre>

    <h3>Running the Application</h3>
    <pre><code># Start MongoDB
mongod

# Start backend (in backend/ directory)
npm run dev

# Start frontend (in frontend/ directory)
npm run dev

# Access application
Frontend: http://localhost:5173
Backend API: http://localhost:5000</code></pre>

    <h2>Project Structure</h2>

    <pre><code>Salesdam-v3/
├── backend/
│   ├── controllers/       # Request handlers
│   ├── models/           # Mongoose schemas
│   ├── routes/           # Express routes
│   ├── middleware/       # Custom middleware
│   ├── utils/            # Utility functions
│   ├── app.js            # Express application
│   └── server.js         # Server entry point
│
├── frontend/
│   ├── src/
│   │   ├── components/   # React components
│   │   ├── pages/        # Page components
│   │   ├── context/      # Context providers
│   │   ├── hooks/        # Custom React hooks
│   │   ├── utils/        # Utility functions
│   │   └── App.jsx       # Root component
│   ├── public/           # Static assets
│   └── index.html        # HTML entry point
│
└── landing/              # Astro landing site
    └── src/
        ├── pages/        # Astro pages
        ├── layouts/      # Layouts
        └── components/   # Astro components</code></pre>

    <h2>Development Workflow</h2>

    <h3>Branch Strategy</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>main:</strong> Production-ready code</li>
      <li><strong>develop:</strong> Integration branch for features</li>
      <li><strong>feature/*:</strong> New features and enhancements</li>
      <li><strong>bugfix/*:</strong> Bug fixes</li>
      <li><strong>hotfix/*:</strong> Critical production fixes</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Commit Conventions</h3>
    <pre><code>feat: Add new feature
fix: Fix bug
docs: Update documentation
style: Code formatting
refactor: Code restructuring
test: Add or update tests
chore: Maintenance tasks</code></pre>

    <h2>Key Concepts</h2>

    <h3>Multi-Tenancy</h3>
    <p>
      Every request is scoped to a tenant (workspace). The <code>tenant</code> middleware
      extracts the tenant ID from the session and adds it to <code
        >req.tenant</code
      >. All database queries must include the tenant filter.
    </p>

    <h3>Dynamic Schema</h3>
    <p>
      Objects and fields are stored as metadata in <code>ObjectMeta</code> and
      <code>FieldMeta</code>. Actual record data is stored in <code
        >DynamicRecord</code
      >
      with a flexible <code>data</code> field (Mongoose Map type).
    </p>

    <h3>Session-Based Authentication</h3>
    <p>
      Uses Express session middleware with MongoDB store. Sessions expire after
      inactivity. The <code>requireAuth</code> middleware protects routes.
    </p>

    <h2>Testing</h2>

    <h3>Running Tests</h3>
    <pre><code># Backend tests
cd backend
npm test

# Frontend tests
cd frontend
npm test

# Run with coverage
npm run test:coverage</code></pre>

    <h3>Test Structure</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Unit Tests:</strong> Individual functions and components</li>
      <li><strong>Integration Tests:</strong> API endpoints and workflows</li>
      <li><strong>E2E Tests:</strong> Full user flows (Cypress/Playwright)</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Deployment</h2>

    <h3>Production Build</h3>
    <pre><code># Build frontend
cd frontend
npm run build

# Frontend build output in frontend/dist/
# Serve static files with Express or CDN</code></pre>

    <h3>Environment Variables</h3>
    <p>Set these in production:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>NODE_ENV=production</code></li>
      <li><code>MONGO_URI</code> - Production MongoDB connection string</li>
      <li><code>SESSION_SECRET</code> - Strong secret key</li>
      <li><code>PORT</code> - Server port (default 5000)</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Contributing</h2>

    <h3>Code Style</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Follow ESLint configuration</li>
      <li>Use meaningful variable names</li>
      <li>Add comments for complex logic</li>
      <li>Write tests for new features</li>
      <li>Update documentation</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Pull Request Process</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Create feature branch from <code>develop</code></li>
      <li>Implement changes with tests</li>
      <li>Run linter and tests</li>
      <li>Update documentation if needed</li>
      <li>Submit PR with clear description</li>
      <li>Address review feedback</li>
      <li>Merge after approval</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Further Reading</h2>

    <div class="guide-grid">
      <a href="/developer/architecture" class="guide-card">
        <h3>Architecture</h3>
        <p>Deep dive into system design and component interactions</p>
      </a>

      <a href="/developer/authentication" class="guide-card">
        <h3>Authentication</h3>
        <p>Session management, middleware, and security</p>
      </a>

      <a href="/developer/data-model" class="guide-card">
        <h3>Data Model</h3>
        <p>Database schemas, relationships, and entity diagrams</p>
      </a>

      <a href="/developer/features" class="guide-card">
        <h3>Features</h3>
        <p>Implementation details for each major feature</p>
      </a>

      <a href="/developer/api" class="guide-card">
        <h3>API Reference</h3>
        <p>Complete endpoint documentation with examples</p>
      </a>

      <a href="/developer/user-stories" class="guide-card">
        <h3>User Stories</h3>
        <p>Complete backlog in sequential build order</p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </ul>

  <style>
    .warning {
      background: #fef3c7;
      border-left: 4px solid #f59e0b;
      padding: 20px;
      margin: 24px 0;
      border-radius: 4px;
      color: var(--text-secondary);
    }

    .warning strong {
      color: #f59e0b;
    }

    .guide-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(280px, 1fr));
      gap: 20px;
      margin: 40px 0;
    }

    .guide-card {
      background: var(--bg);
      padding: 24px;
      border-radius: 12px;
      border: 2px solid var(--border);
      transition: all 0.3s;
    }

    .guide-card:hover {
      transform: translateY(-4px);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow-lg);
      border-color: var(--primary);
    }

    .guide-card h3 {
      margin: 0 0 12px 0;
      color: var(--text);
      font-size: 1.25rem;
    }

    .guide-card p {
      color: var(--text-secondary);
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      line-height: 1.6;
      margin: 0;
    }
  </style>
</DevLayout>
